    "## Exercise 1\n",
    "### 1a: Variable selection and sample restriction\n",
    "First, we remove observations before year 2000, then we select ten stock-level characteristics based on the variable-importance results in @Gu.2020, Figure 5. The selected variables cover price trends: `mom1m`, `mom12m`, size and liquidity: `mvel1`, `turn`, risk and volatility: `beta`\n",
    "`retvol`, and valuation/fundamentals: `bm`, `ep`, `roaq`, `invest`.\n",
    "\n",
    "For the macroeconomic state variables from @Goyal.2008 library, we follow @Gu.2020 Table 4 and include aggregate book-to-market (`bm`), the Treasury bill rate (`tbl`), the default yield spread (`dfy`), and the term spread (`tms`). These variables capture aggregate valuation, interest rate conditions, credit risk, and the slope of the yield curve."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "1232d9ff",
   "metadata": {
    "cache": false
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#df = pd.read_parquet(\"/Users/AstridMoeller/Documents/GitHub/AEF-git/data-python/stock_characteristics_monthly.parquet\")\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.read_parquet(\"/Users/AstridMoeller/AEF/data/stock_characteristics_monthly.parquet\")\n",
    "df.head()\n",
    "\n",
    "# keep observations from January 2000 onward\n",
    "df[\"date\"] = pd.to_datetime(df[\"date\"])\n",
    "df = df.loc[df[\"date\"] >= \"2000-01-01\"].copy()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "62f29237",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "stock_chars = [\n",
    "    \"characteristic_mom1m\",    # short-term reversal (price trend)\n",
    "    \"characteristic_mom12m\",   # 12-month momentum (price trend)\n",
    "    \"characteristic_mvel1\",    # size (liquidity)\n",
    "    \"characteristic_turn\",     # share turnover (liquidity)\n",
    "    \"characteristic_beta\",     # market beta (risk)\n",
    "    \"characteristic_retvol\",   # return volatility (risk)\n",
    "    \"characteristic_bm\",       # book-to-market (value)\n",
    "    \"characteristic_ep\",       # earnings-to-price (value)\n",
    "    \"characteristic_roaq\",     # profitability\n",
    "    \"characteristic_invest\",   # investment growth\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "macro_vars = [\n",
    "    \"macro_bm\",    # aggregate book-to-market\n",
    "    \"macro_tbl\",   # T-bill rate\n",
    "    \"macro_dfy\",   # default yield spread\n",
    "    \"macro_tms\",   # term spread\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "base_cols = [\"permno\", \"date\", \"ret_excess\", \"mktcap_lag\", \"sic2\"]\n",
    "df = df[base_cols + stock_chars + macro_vars].copy()"
   ]
  },
