   "source": [
    "Using the fitted models, we generate predicted excess returns for each stock-month observation in the validation and test samples. These predictions reflect expected returns based on firm characteristics, macroeconomic variables, and their interactions.\n",
    "The predictions are used to rank stocks in portfolio construction, where higher predicted returns correspond to higher deciles and more attractive investment opportunities.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Exercise 3b: Decile portfolio sorts"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 21,
   "id": "1944fde3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#| output: false\n",
    "\n",
    "def assign_deciles(df, pred_col, decile_col):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Assign stocks to decile portfolios each month based on predicted returns.\n",
    "    Uses ranked predictions to avoid qcut dropping bins when many values are tied.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    df = df.copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "    def month_deciles(x):\n",
    "        if x.notna().sum() < 10:\n",
    "            return pd.Series(np.nan, index=x.index)\n",
    "\n",
    "        ranked = x.rank(method=\"first\")\n",
    "        return pd.qcut(ranked, 10, labels=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "    df[decile_col] = df.groupby(\"date\")[pred_col].transform(month_deciles)\n",
    "    df[decile_col] = pd.to_numeric(df[decile_col], errors=\"coerce\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    return df\n",
    "\n",
    "meta_val = assign_deciles(meta_val, \"pred_en\", \"decile_en\")\n",
    "meta_val = assign_deciles(meta_val, \"pred_rf\", \"decile_rf\")\n",
    "\n",
    "meta_test = assign_deciles(meta_test, \"pred_en\", \"decile_en\")\n",
    "meta_test = assign_deciles(meta_test, \"pred_rf\", \"decile_rf\")"
   ]
  },
